# The program runs `for (const [i, v] of list.entries())` over a value that is declared as an array of numbers. The loop is versioned.
# The specialized version is entered if the array is pristine and holds numbers.
# It steps by index alone, the pattern takes the index and the element as they are, and the sum is an addition of numbers.
# The cleanup of the pattern is nested under the cleanup of the for-of, outside the loop, and it is visited alongside each version. Any other value takes the loop as written.
# Fault injection, testing=SkipPairGuard: the pattern takes the two parts no matter what is iterated.
# For the array of a subclass that has `entries` of its own, nothing was stored into the parts, so the program silently prints a wrong result.
# Where the walk checks its proofs, the type of the iterated value is tested again, separately from the guard that the fault drops. With both switches the program crashes with a named error.
# A second fault injection, testing=AssumePristineReceivers: where a method call that the walk can see opens the iteration, the check that the array is pristine is assumed to pass.
# The array of a subclass that has `entries` of its own is then stepped by index, and the program silently prints a wrong result.
# Where the walk checks its proofs, that check is made again after the iteration opens, once per loop. With both switches the program crashes with a named error.
# f1 = each
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(TYPED): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# TYPED-LABEL: code f1:Body
# TYPED: = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Double level=Proven
# TYPED: number @Double = Add {{*}}form=Numbers
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 37.5 36 0 50.5 NaN 00a10b
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# NONE: 37.5 36 0 50.5 NaN 00a10b
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipPairGuard
# LIE: 37.5 36 0 NaN NaN 00a10b
# LIE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipPairGuard,CheckProofsAtRunTime
